+### 2030 — A read that did not finish is not a mismatch, and quarantine cannot tell the difference on its own
+
+- FINDING: `PutBlob` routed EVERY non-`ErrUnsafeOwnership` inspection error to `quarantineExisting`. `inspectExisting` returned raw `os.Open`, `io.Copy` and `Close` errors, so at the decision point an EMFILE or a transient I/O error was indistinguishable from a hash mismatch. A flaky read on the existing digest-path entry permanently moved a VALID immutable object out of the namespace. SPEC.md:819-820 authorizes quarantine for "a hash mismatch or representation disagreement" only, and a read that never completed proves neither.
+- FINDING: the projection already got this right — `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` classified a failed read as `sourceFailure` and refused. The two paths disagreed, and the store side is the one that moves data. Nothing in the package made them agree; they were two independent open/copy/hash blocks that happened to be written by different hands.
+- DECISION: extracted `verifyBlobContent` in `internal/localstore/blob_inspection.go` as the single owner of "read this digest-path entry and report what that proved", returning a `blobVerdict` whose zero value `blobUnproven` is deliberately not a proof. Both `inspectExisting` and `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` now consult it; each still maps the verdict onto its own consequence, so the projection's two `projectionRefusal` call sites stay in `projection.go` where the derived refusal inventory can still demand a negative path for them.
+- DECISION: `blobVerdict.quarantineWarranted()` is the one predicate authorizing a move, and only `blobMismatch` satisfies it. `resolveExistingEntry` funnels BOTH the first-attempt and the raced post-rename branches, which previously carried two hand-copied classification blocks that could drift apart independently.
+- DECISION: `storeOperations.openExisting` and `projectionHooks.openBlob` are injected read seams. Without them the transient-failure path needs real descriptor exhaustion or media failure, which is why the original auditor could only argue the defect rather than reproduce it.
+- EVIDENCE: 5 mutants, 5 killed; baseline and restored tree both exit 0. Collapsing the classification back (delete the `blobUnreadable` branch, gate quarantine on `verdict == blobUnsafe`) reddens 3 of 4 injected-failure subtests plus the store/projection agreement assertion. Widening `quarantineWarranted` to "any verdict that is not a match" reddens the three pre-existing unsafe-entry tests — the unsafe entry starts getting moved. Narrowing it to `false` and narrowing the mismatch comparison to size-only both redden `TestPutBlobQuarantinesBothInputsWhenExistingDigestPathIsCorrupt`; the size-only mutant is the one that proves the same-size digest disagreement is a real bound, not a delete-only artifact. Making `scanAuthoritativeBlobs` ignore `hooks.openBlob` reddens the agreement test alone, which is what keeps that test from passing on a seam the projection never consults. Evidence: `BUG-260902-1qsdag_mutant-evidence-final.log`.
+- NOTE: the agreement is asserted, not assumed. `TestObjectStoreAndProjectionAgreeOnIncompleteReadVersusProvenMismatch` drives `PutBlob` and `openProjection` over the same two on-disk conditions and fails if their proven-mismatch classification differs, if the projection ever moves a durable object, or if the store moves one without a completed disagreeing read.
+- SCOPE: `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`, `internal/localstore/blob_inspection.go`, `internal/localstore/blob_inspection_test.go`, `internal/localstore/object_store.go`, `internal/localstore/projection.go`, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json`, `internal/traceability/traceability.go`
